    "created_at": "2016-08-30T04:32:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-30T04:32:35Z",
    "body": "The basic idea when we hashed this out was that we would generally err on the side of throwing, since it gives engines maximum implementational flexibility (and diminishes web-compat constraints), and we're not really trying to make these objects friendly to operate on.\n\nI don't really remember the specifics of |delete|, but it doesn't surprise me that we decided it should throw.\n\nThe implementation in Firefox is here: http://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/0dd403224a5acb0702bdbf7ff405067f5d29c239/js/xpconnect/wrappers/FilteringWrapper.cpp#235\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
